:: kavya_first_arjun_body
<div class="intimate"><span class="tag">Intimate · body discovery</span>
<<img "kavya_first_arjun_body.png" "admin access, at last">>
<b>Height.</b> The world rearranges. Temple walls that loomed are at eye level. The Nandi statue you looked up at thirty seconds ago looks at you straight on. Everything above your former eye-line has dropped six inches, and the effect is like stepping onto a stage.

You look at your hands. Arjun's hands. You spread the fingers wide and the reach is obscene   thumb to pinkie, easily nine inches. Where your hands stretched and repositioned on every keyboard, these would //rest// on a full-size QWERTY. A callus on the right index from mouse-clicking. These hands have written code. They know.

You make fists. Substantial. Dense. When you curl these fingers the force feels concentrated   the difference between a slap and a punch built into the architecture.

Voice. You clear your throat: a drum struck in a larger chamber. "Testing." A full octave below your usual register, the vibration starting in the //chest//, radiating through a wider ribcage. You feel your own voice in your collarbones for the first time in your life.

Flat chest. The absence of breast weight is   you lack the adjective. Like removing a backpack you wore so long you forgot it was there. You roll your shoulders and nothing moves except muscle and bone.

And between your legs: weight. Mass. Presence. Warm, soft, constant. Your female anatomy is internal, folded, hidden. This is external, hanging, negotiating with fabric and gravity in a running dialogue you can feel with every micro-adjustment. You shift your weight and the testicles shift too, rolling slightly, and you catalogue it with fascinated horror.

<div class="dialogue">"How does it feel?"</div>

"Like having admin access. After three years of read-only."

<div class="thought kavya">Twelve hours. Do not waste a minute of them.</div>
</div>

