:: kavya_pulsar_ride_d3
<div class="intimate"><span class="tag">Intimate</span>
<<img "kavya_pulsar_ride.png" "Pune, 5:25 AM">>
Pune at 5:25   near-empty, streetlights on damp asphalt. You lean into it. The wind hits Arjun's face and there's no dupatta to manage, no hair whipping into your mouth. His hair is short enough that the air passes //through// it. The air moves over you instead of around you. Narrower wind profile.

You open the throttle. The Pulsar responds and for one exhilarating moment   engine screaming in second, speedo past forty, dawn painting the sky Pune-orange   you feel what this body was built for. Motion. Velocity. A body that takes up space and moves through it with a confidence that has nothing to do with the mind driving it.

Freedom tastes like morning air and engine exhaust and a face nobody is watching.
</div>
