:: kavya_laptop_first_touch_d3
<<img "pg_room_kavya_pov.png" "the keyboard, finally">>
The screen wakes. VS Code, still open from last night, a half-finished DBMS query on line 47. A full-size mechanical keyboard on USB, not the laptop's built-in. Dual monitors.

Your fingers   Arjun's fingers   settle on the home row. F and J, the dimples under your index fingers. Every key exactly where it's always been on every keyboard, but //this// one has switches that respond with a click you feel in your fingertips and in your heart.

You don't code yet. You just rest your hands there for a minute, on a real machine, in a body that fits it, and let one tear escape   Arjun's single, reluctant, bureaucratically-processed tear.

Then you notice a folder on the desktop: <b>Important Documents</b>. And you notice you want to open it.

