:: kavya_coding_ecstasy_d3
<div class="intimate"><span class="tag">The emotional payoff</span>
<<img "kavya_coding_joy.png" "CS lab, real hardware">>
Terminal 6, closest to the wall, screen angled away. A Dell that doesn't wheeze at JavaScript. Dual monitors. A mechanical keyboard whose switches you feel in your fingertips and in your heart.

Your fingers   Arjun's fingers   settle on the home row. F and J. The dimples under your index fingers. Every key exactly where it's always been on every keyboard, but //this// one responds with a click.

You build the medical-imaging classifier you've been carrying around in your head for a year. Two hours pass and you don't notice   nothing exists except syntax and logic and the euphoria of making something that WORKS. When you surface, the training pipeline runs. The metrics are clean.

One tear escapes. You wipe it with the back of a hand that's bigger than your face used to be.

<div class="thought kavya">You will lose this at 8 PM. You know that. You're doing it anyway, as hard and as fast as you can, because a thing you did once is a thing you did.</div>
</div>

